# BYD Shark 6 Performance — Build & Payload

## Status
Decision resolved (2026-06-25): buy and build as configured, defer GVM upgrade. Awaiting order
confirmation, charger install, and a post-build weighbridge check.

## Summary
Buy-and-build decision for a BYD Shark 6 Performance PHEV dual-cab ute with a touring fitout (RAID
bull bar, glass canopy, roof racks, drawers, fridge). The live question was payload headroom and
GVM-upgrade timing. Worked out: factory payload 725 kg (GVM 3,500 − kerb 2,775); ~265 kg of
accessories/fitout leaves ~460 kg, which is ample for Nick's real use (1–2 occupants). GVM upgrade
(to 3,850 kg, +350 kg payload) is deferrable. Full detail, build cost, and payload tables live at
`~/Documents/workspace/projects/byd-shark-6/README.md`.

## System Prompt
When Nick raises this project, read the workspace README first — it holds the build list, the
payload maths, and the resolved decision. Two standing caveats to surface whenever loading, towing,
or the GVM upgrade come up: (1) axle limits (GAWR), not just GVM, may bind first — heavy kit sits at
the ends, so the rear axle is the likely constraint; recommend a public weighbridge axle-by-axle on
the built rig before trusting the headline payload. (2) A post-registration GVM upgrade costs more
than a pre-rego one (individual engineering certification, state-dependent in VIC), so "later" is
not free. Metric units, Australian English, recommendation-first. No dedicated agent; mint one via
agent-onboarder only if this becomes recurring.

## Key facts
- Variant: BYD Shark 6 **Performance** (PHEV).
- GVM 3,500 kg; kerb 2,775 kg; factory payload 725 kg; braked tow 2,500 kg.
- Accessory/fitout total ~265 kg → ~460 kg payload remaining.
- Confirmed component weights: RAID bull bar ~65 kg, glass canopy ~65 kg, drawers 70 kg, roof racks
  25 kg, fridge 30 kg empty (+10–15 loaded). AC charger is wall-mounted (0 kg on vehicle).
- Build subtotal ~$82,549 (vehicle + options, ex on-roads, ex charger install, ex drawers/fridge).

